1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,639
European Union lawmakers gave final approval to the 27 nation groups artificial intelligence

2
00:00:07,639 --> 00:00:13,519
law Wednesday. The rules are expected to take effect later this year.

3
00:00:15,339 --> 00:00:21,600
Lawmakers in the European Parliament voted in favor of the Artificial Intelligence Act

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:29,399
five years after regulations were first proposed. Major technology companies have generally

5
00:00:29,399 --> 00:00:36,179
supported the idea. But they want to make sure new AI requirements work in their favor.

6
00:00:37,439 --> 00:00:44,020
Open AI Chief Sam Altman suggested the maker of ChatGPT might pull out of Europe

7
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:51,380
if it cannot comply with the AI Act. He later said his company had no plans to leave.

8
00:00:52,340 --> 00:01:00,420
Here are some details about Europe's new AI rules. Like many EU regulations, the AI Act

9
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:08,120
started as consumer safety legislation. The EU took a risk-based approach to products or services

10
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:17,599
that use artificial intelligence or AI. If an AI application is risky, then more rules cover it.

11
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:24,340
Most AI systems are expected to be low-risk like content's recommendation systems

12
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:31,680
or filters that block spam or unwanted email. Companies can choose to follow voluntary

13
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:40,480
requirements and codes of conduct. High-risk uses of AI include tools used in medical devices

14
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:45,140
or important infrastructure like water or electrical networks.

15
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:52,200
Those face additional requirements like using what the legislation calls high-quality data

16
00:01:52,719 --> 00:02:00,379
and providing clear information to users. Some AI uses are banned because they are considered

17
00:02:00,379 --> 00:02:08,020
to present an unacceptable risk. Those include things like social scoring systems that are meant

18
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:15,580
to govern how people behave. Some sorts of predictive policing and emotion recognition systems

19
00:02:16,099 --> 00:02:25,120
also are reportedly banned in schools and workplaces. Other banned uses include ones that police use

20
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:32,139
to scan faces in public places using AI-powered remote biometric identification systems.

21
00:02:32,939 --> 00:02:37,960
There is an exception for use in serious crimes like kidnapping or terrorism.

22
00:02:40,219 --> 00:02:46,740
The laws early versions centered on AI systems that carry out limited tasks like

23
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:55,580
reviewing employment information and job applications. But general AI models like open AI's

24
00:02:55,580 --> 00:03:04,560
chat GPT forced EU officials to add rules for generative AI models. AI chatbot systems that can

25
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:11,680
produce life-like responses, images and more are examples of generative AI models.

26
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:20,080
Developers of general-purpose AI models will have to provide detailed descriptions of the writings,

27
00:03:20,639 --> 00:03:26,960
pictures, video and other data on the internet that was used to train the systems.

28
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:31,020
They must also follow EU copyright law.

29
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:40,719
AI-generated pictures, video or audio of existing people, places or events must be labeled as

30
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:48,439
artificially produced. These sorts of media are known as deepfakes because they appear to show

31
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:56,340
real people doing or saying things that are not real. There are reportedly extra rules

32
00:03:56,340 --> 00:04:06,020
for the biggest and most powerful AI models that carry systemic risks. Those include open AI's GPT-4

33
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:14,520
and Google's Gemini. The EU first suggested AI regulations in 2019.

34
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:20,699
Europe was quick to propose rules for the new and developing industry.

35
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:28,300
In the US, President Joe Biden signed an executive order on AI in October.

36
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:32,920
The US Congress is likely to propose legislation.

37
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:39,720
Lawmakers in at least seven US states are working on their own AI legislation.

38
00:04:40,439 --> 00:04:43,899
And international agreements are possible too.

39
00:04:46,019 --> 00:04:53,519
Chinese President Xi Jinping has proposed his global AI governance initiative for fair and safe

40
00:04:53,519 --> 00:04:59,980
use of AI. Other major countries including Brazil and Japan are

41
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,839
are developing rules as are the United Nations and group of seven industrialized nations.

42
00:05:09,319 --> 00:05:16,040
The AI Act is expected to officially become law by May or June, after approval from EU

43
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:16,920
member countries.

44
00:05:18,139 --> 00:05:20,660
Rules will start taking effect slowly.

45
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:28,019
Countries will be required to ban unapproved AI systems six months after the law takes

46
00:05:28,019 --> 00:05:28,480
effect.

47
00:05:30,139 --> 00:05:37,000
Rules for general-purpose AI systems like chatbots will start going into effect in one year.

48
00:05:37,939 --> 00:05:44,480
By the middle of 2026, the complete set of regulations, including requirements for high-risk

49
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:46,339
systems, will be in effect.

50
00:05:47,939 --> 00:05:52,439
Each EU country will set up their own AI enforcement agency.

51
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:59,100
Citizens can make a complaint if they think they have been the victim of a violation of

52
00:05:59,100 --> 00:05:59,639
the rules.

53
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:08,199
And the EU will create an AI office that will oversee the law for general-purpose AI systems.

54
00:06:09,759 --> 00:06:18,120
Violations of the AI Act could be punished with a fine of up to $38 million, or 7% of

55
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,000
a company's worldwide revenue.

56
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,660
I'm Dan Novak.

